{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise CONFIRMED in code, with a nuance worth recording.\n\nThe wasted-spend gap is NARROWER than 'plan unchanged since a BLOCK': reuse.verdict_reuse already short-circuits the wholly-unchanged case at zero LLM cost, but it requires the ENTIRE material fingerprint AND the review code SHA to hold still. Touch a file_impact row or land an unrelated commit and it correctly declines, so the ticket pays a full multi-pass review even though the plan prose the blocking findings quoted was never edited. That residue is what this pre-check warns on.\n\nBoth inputs the plan assumed exist and are persisted: the v2 sidecar records each finding's Pass-1 'evidence' grounding quotes (story 4e19, lossless) and the per-component 'material_parts' (bug 94a3). No cited-anchor/unchanged-plan pre-check existed.\n\nImplementation: new module src/rebar/llm/plan_review/cited_anchor.py holds all logic, because the hook point (_run_plan_review in plan_review/__init__.py) was at 786/800 LOC against the module-size gate. Wiring there is 4 lines (now 793/800). The warning fires only when (1) the latest sidecar verdict is BLOCK with blocking findings, (2) the recorded 'description' component digest equals the current one, and (3) at least one cited anchor is still present verbatim. Condition 2 is what makes condition 3 sound: the sidecar stores the description's fingerprint, not its bytes, so reasoning about 'the text the finding quoted' is valid precisely because that text has not moved.\n\nWARN-ONLY contract honored: logger.warning only, placed after verdict_reuse and BEFORE drift_refresh so it precedes any billable call; returns a metrics record, never a verdict; no new flag, no decline, no exit-code change. metrics.precheck.cited_anchor_warning is stamped on EVERY review (False is a measurement, not an absence) so precision is computable offline per ADR 0054.\n\nGates green locally: 17 new tests pass; 898 passed / 4 skipped across plan_review+sidecar+reuse (no verdict-shape regression); make lint and make typecheck clean.\n\nPushed as Gerrit change 1631."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786513885738207001,"uuid":"74fce5e6-0761-43ed-8851-61e73eabfd4d"}